---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <title>How it works | Spokane Contractors</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Browse Spokane contractors for free with no sign-in. Save favorites on your device and contact listings directly."
    />
  </Fragment>

  <article class="how-it-works">
    <p class="hero-eyebrow">Simple by design</p>
    <h1>How it works</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Spokane Contractors is a free local directory. Browse listings, open a
      profile, and contact the business—without creating an account.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>No sign-in required</h2>
      <p>
        You do not need to register, log in, or leave an email to use this site.
        There is no paywall and no “create a free account to continue” step.
        Search, filter, call, and email from the listing itself.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Find a contractor</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Filter by trade, city, or rating—or search by name.</li>
        <li>Open <strong>View profile</strong> for full contact details, license info when available, and Google Business links.</li>
        <li>Tap a phone number to call, or use email and website links when listed.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Save with the heart</h2>
      <p>
        Tap the heart on a listing to save it. Open the <a href="/?view=saved">Saved</a> tab anytime to revisit your shortlist.
      </p>
      <p>
        Saves live in this browser on this device only (local storage). That keeps
        the directory free of accounts while still letting you bookmark contractors
        while you compare options.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Limits of device saves</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Saved lists do not sync to your phone, another computer, or another browser.</li>
        <li>Clearing site data, cookies, or using private/incognito mode can erase saves.</li>
        <li>If you switch devices, start a fresh shortlist—or share listing links with yourself.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Before you hire</h2>
      <p>
        Listings are a starting point. Confirm licensing, insurance, and scope of
        work directly with the contractor before signing a contract.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>For contractors</h2>
      <p>
        Google Business Profile is the source of truth for listing details. Keep
        your GBP accurate, then <a href="/get-listed">request to be added</a> (or
        tell us something looks wrong). We refresh the directory from GBP as
        needed—we don’t maintain a separate editable profile here.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="how-actions">
      <a class="button button-primary" href="/">Browse contractors</a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/get-listed">Get listed</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
